      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T09:11:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unlike the other Intel platforms the Baytrail GPIO is a `bool`:\n```\ndrivers/pinctrl/intel/Kconfig:config PINCTRL_BAYTRAIL\ndrivers/pinctrl/intel/Kconfig-  bool \"Intel Baytrail GPIO pin control\"\ndrivers/pinctrl/intel/Kconfig-  select PINCTRL_INTEL\n```\nYeah, it would be better to have it in the vendor space, but IMO changing config type to `tristate` (if we decide to do that) should go to the upstream not ACK. With such change in the upstream we probably can `select PINCTRL_INTEL` as GKI hidden and than GPIO drivers for all Intel platforms can be moved to the vendor.",
      "parentUuid": "bc44c7de_1c0351ae",
